      "side": 1,
      "message": "`BeginOfThisString * sizeof(wchar_t)` can overflow here, resulting in an incorrect `StrW` offset.\n\nFor example, if `Offset` is read as a small value (e.g., `0`), `BeginOfThisString \u003d Offset - SizeOfHeader - 8` can underflow to a very large value, which will then overflow when multiplied by `sizeof(wchar_t)`. \nAdditionally, if `BeginOfThisString` is large, `EndOfThisString \u003d BeginOfThisString + Len` could wrap around, causing `LargestPosition` to be under-calculated and bypassing the later `WideSizeOfTag` overflow check.\n\nAdding an overflow check for `BeginOfThisString * sizeof(wchar_t)` similar to the one for `WideLen` above would protect `StrW` and also ensure `EndOfThisString` does not wrap around.\n\nSuggestion:\n```c\n        cmsUInt32Number WideOffset \u003d BeginOfThisString * sizeof(wchar_t);\n        if (WideOffset / sizeof(wchar_t) !\u003d BeginOfThisString) goto Error;\n        mlu -\u003eEntries[i].StrW \u003d WideOffset / sizeof(cmsUInt16Number);\n```",
